# Polychkova

Tier list app. Planned work: `ROADMAP.md`.

## Agent communication

- Terse, technical, no-fluff responses.
- Lead with the result; include evidence or commands when useful.

## Before changing code

- Read sibling files; match naming, layout, patterns.
- Smallest correct diff. No drive-by refactors.
- New dependency → concrete reason; flag before adding. Use `pnpm add` / `pnpm add -D`.

## Simplicity

- Prefer less code: delete/simplify before new hooks, listeners, deps.
- Passing CI does not justify extra machinery.

## Docs and comments

- Repo docs are specifications, not agent memory. Never persist guidance inferred from the current
  or recent work, including generalized versions of its problems, fixes, or implementation choices.
- Edit `.cursor/rules/**` only when the user explicitly asks to establish or revise a specific
  durable policy. Do not treat a request to implement, debug, explain, or update docs as permission
  to create repository guidance.
- Behavior, env, or CI changes → update `README.md` in the same change.
- `ROADMAP.md` for planned work; remove items when shipped.
- Comments: why non-obvious, not what the code already says.

## Quality bar

- Complete, working changes for requested scope only.
- Root-cause only — no `@ts-ignore`, blanket lint disables, stub returns, config loosening.
- Proper fix blocked → stop and report.

## Verification

Before done:

```shell
pnpm verify
```

## Env & secrets

- Never commit `.env` / `.env.local`.
- API keys server-only — not `NEXT_PUBLIC_*` unless truly public.
- Document new environment variables in `.env.example`.

## Git

- Never commit, stage, or push. User runs all git ops.
